<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40139" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιμειδ-άω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>smile at</i> or <i>upon</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always in phrase, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δ᾽</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιμειδήσας προσέφη</span> he addressed
			him <i>with a smile</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.356
			</span></i>, al.; in <i><span class="en">
				10.400
			</span></i>, of a scornful smile; but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦκ᾽ ἐπιμειδήσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					547
				</span></i>
			: c.dat., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.345
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
